# Privacy Policy
Last updated August 30 2026

Rydex Terms of Service https://github.com/gurjap-og/Terms_Of_Services/blob/main/Terms-Of-Services

### 1. Introduction
Thanks for checking out Rydex. Before you use the bot please read and accept the Terms of Service of the bot and then this Privacy Policy.

Your privacy matters to me. This document explains exactly how your data is used when you use the Rydex bot in a Discord server.

When I say server admins I mean anyone in a Discord server who can use Rydex configuration commands either because they already have the right permissions or because someone with higher permissions gave them access for example through noprefix.

### 2. Summary
I have not been collecting personalized data for advertising or marketing and I never sell your data. The information I store is used only to make the Rydex features work and to keep improving the Rydex bot. Most of what gets saved is data that you or your server admins actively create containers welcome messages moderation cases voice channel setups giveaways anti nuke settings role and autorole rules and so on.

If your server turns on Server Logs Rydex will forward live event data including the content of deleted or edited messages to the log channel your admins set up. I don't keep a separate copy of that content in my own database it's only sent to the channel you chose.

### 3. How Rydex Uses Data Inside Discord
When you add Rydex to your server you allow me to see and process the server information the bot can access so it can provide the features below.

**3.1 Container Builder**
Rydex lets you build and send custom Components V2 message layouts. When you save a container I store its name the guild ID accent color and the full layout data text images buttons so it can be recalled edited or resent later. If a container has interactive buttons I also store the button's custom ID guild ID and the action it performs. When a container is sent to a channel I record the guild ID channel ID message ID and layout data so the message can be tracked or edited afterward.

**3.2 Welcome System**
If your server enables welcome messages I store the welcome configuration for that server whether it's enabled the destination channel accent color layout data auto delete settings an optional auto role ID and if you turn them on a DM welcome message and milestone announcement settings for example every 100th member. This data is used only to greet new members the way you have configured.

**3.3 Join to Create (J2C)**
If you set up Join to Create voice channels I store the join and control channel IDs each temporary voice channel's owner member limit bitrate region and lock ghost NSFW waiting room and thread flags. I also store per user preferences name patterns saved templates any users a channel owner has blocked or trusted any server wide J2C blacklist entries with reason if provided and a running count of channels created per server. All of this is used only to recreate your voice setup and enforce the owner controls block trust limit lock and so on.

**3.4 Moderation**
When your server uses Rydex's moderation commands timeout kick masskick ban tempban softban unban purge warn and so on I log each action as a case the action taken the target user's ID and tag the moderator's ID the reason given and a timestamp. This history is only used to power the case and modlog commands inside your server. Warnings are stored separately per member with the moderator ID reason and timestamp. If your server sets up a jail role I store that role ID and, whenever a member is jailed, that member's previous roles so they can be correctly restored when unjailed. Scheduled temp bans are stored with an unban time so the ban can be automatically lifted.

**3.5 Anti Nuke**
If your server enables the anti nuke system I store the on or off status for the server, which of the 16 monitored filters ban kick prune member update role and channel create delete update webhook create delete update bot add guild update and mention spam are turned on, and the punishment configured for each filter (ban, kick, or stripstaff). I also store a whitelist of users, bots, and roles exempt from anti nuke actions per filter, and a list of extra Anti Nuke admins your server has granted access to. This data is only used to run the protection system in your server. Anti Nuke does not currently keep a running history log of past triggers or store event thresholds beyond the enabled/disabled filter toggles described above.

**3.6 Server Logs**
If you enable Server Logs Rydex listens for the server events you've chosen to log message edits and deletes member joins and leaves role changes channel changes and so on and posts a formatted summary including message content for edits and deletes when available to the log channels you configured. The relay happens in real time. I don't store a second copy of that content in Rydex's database only your per server configuration which channels map to which events and which events are turned off is saved.

**3.7 Giveaways**
If you run a giveaway through Rydex I store the prize description image URL host ID winner count timing and status plus the user IDs of everyone who enters and every winner selected. This lets entries be tracked and re rolled if needed.

**3.8 Role Management**
When server admins use Rydex's role commands to give remove toggle or bulk apply roles, or to clear all roles from a member, these actions are performed live against Discord and are not separately logged or stored by Rydex.

**3.9 Autorole**
If your server sets up autorole I store which roles are auto assigned on join, whether each rule targets all members, bots only, or humans only, and whether the system is enabled. This is used only to apply the roles you've configured whenever someone joins.

**3.10 Custom Prefix**
Each server can set its own command prefix. I store the guild ID and the chosen prefix so Rydex responds to the right one in your server.

**3.11 Owner and Administrative Tools**
For bot owner administration I keep a no prefix access list who can run commands without a prefix who granted it and for how long, and separate logs of owner level actions such as leaving a server, generating a server invite, or listing servers, and of bot reboots, including who performed the action, the server affected where relevant, and when. This is only for administrative accountability and is not used to monitor normal user activity.

### 4. Discord Permissions and Intents
To work properly Rydex requests these privileged intents from Discord

Server Members Intent used to identify members for permission checks auto role and autorole on join anti nuke exemption checks and owner or no prefix authorization

Message Content Intent used to read prefix command invocations for example .help or .container and when Server Logs is enabled to relay edited or deleted message content to your configured log channel

Voice States used to detect users joining or leaving Join to Create channels so temporary channels can be created managed and cleaned up

I only use these intents for the purposes described in this policy. I do not use them for bulk data harvesting.

### 5. What I Do Not Collect
I do not read log or store the general content of your messages outside the specific features listed above container builder welcome DMs moderation reasons anti nuke configuration and the Server Logs relay

I do not collect Discord presence data online offline or idle status

I do not collect any payment information Rydex is free to use

I do not knowingly collect data from users under the age of 13 or the higher minimum age required by Discord's Terms of Service in your region

### 6. Basic Technical Data
I collect aggregate uptime latency ping and system resource usage CPU and memory for Rydex's own status and stats commands. This data describes the bot's host not individual users and is never tied to any person.

### 7. Security
The servers and databases that power Rydex are not publicly accessible. I do my best to keep everything secure but no method of electronic storage or transmission is 100 percent safe and I cannot guarantee absolute data security. I am not liable for any data loss or data breach.

### 8. How Long Data Is Kept and How to Delete It
Container welcome J2C moderation anti nuke giveaway role autorole server log configuration and prefix data are stored per server and stay until you delete them with the relevant bot command the associated container channel or giveaway is removed or Rydex is removed from the server.

When you remove Rydex from a server the associated data for that server may be deleted during routine cleanup though this is not guaranteed to happen immediately. Owner level administrative logs no prefix grants reboot and action logs are kept for as long as reasonably needed for accountability.

Unless stated otherwise data is not automatically deleted from Rydex's servers. If you want something removed contact me through the support server below and include your Discord user ID not just your username.

### 9. Children's Privacy
Rydex is not directed at children under 13. Discord itself requires users to meet a minimum age please check Discord's Terms of Service for the exact rules in your region. If I become aware that I have collected data from someone below the applicable minimum age I will delete it.

### 10. Changes to This Policy
I may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. When I make material changes I'll update the Last updated date at the top. Continuing to use Rydex after changes take effect means you accept the revised policy.

